From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:54:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_z2: Settle a D21 for 2260 ms before the touch
 arm by default

A D21 started with the working configuration still delivered no frames
until it rested 2260 ms (the gap iOS leaves) and got a second wake
before the touch arm. On the contributor's iPhone 8 Plus, three
start-ups without the wait stayed silent; the first with it reported
touches. Make that the default instead of a module parameter to set.

It is a fixed wait, not a readiness check: what the controller waits
for is unknown, so it should become a check once that is found.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
index 8fb33b202..1cf8a18cb 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
@@ -3918,10 +3918,17 @@ static int apple_z2_gen2_send_calibration(struct apple_z2 *z2,
 }
 
 /* Reads a report @times times if the controller has it; absent is fine. */
-static unsigned int d21_settle_ms;
+/*
+ * A D21 only starts reporting when it rests this long after its configuration,
+ * then gets a second wake, before the touch arm: 2260 ms is the gap iOS (JADE)
+ * leaves there. Without it every start-up tested stayed silent. This is a fixed
+ * wait, not a readiness check: what the controller is waiting for is unknown,
+ * and the wait should become a check on that once it is found.
+ */
+static unsigned int d21_settle_ms = 2260;
 module_param(d21_settle_ms, uint, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(d21_settle_ms,
-		 "D21: settle this long, then wake, before the touch arm (JADE: 2260; 0: off)");
+		 "D21: settle this long, then wake, before the touch arm (default 2260 as on iOS; 0: off)");
 
 static int apple_z2_gen2_read_optional(struct apple_z2 *z2, u8 report,
 				       unsigned int times, const char *tag)
